  "findings": [
    "One raw harness completion (request turn 45 / scored assistant turn 46) has neither content nor tool calls. Direct SSE reproduction generated 1024 tokens, forced tool_call_close_forcing, and reported private finish_details.reason=invalid_tool_call but public finish_reason=stop; no visible content or tool call was emitted.",
    "23/26 nonempty turns have COMPLETE timestamps preceding RECV_FIRST by 0.078-0.126ms. Upstream session.py uses worker resp.completed_at for COMPLETE and coordinator now_ns for RECV_FIRST. TPOT is invalid and must not be inverted into decode tok/s.",
    "Direct first-turn SSE diagnostic emits role immediately and the whole malformed tool-markup text near completion. This endpoint behavior also prevents token-level TTFT/TPOT interpretation.",
    "Two harness completions finish length; another empty completion is stop despite the server reporting 1024 generated tokens. Some nonempty responses contain tool-like markup as content rather than structured calls.",
    "Canonical client tokenizer metrics and engine token counts differ; e.g. first prompt 1363 vs 1383. Do not equate client visible-output TPS to engine decode speed.",
    "All 27 replay requests increment host_sampler_requests and zero increment MTP requests. The probe identifies stop/repair sequences and tool_call_constraint as sampler blockers."
  ],
